# Specify files that shouldn't be modified by Fern

# src/main/java/com/whop/api/helpers/oidc is the hand-written OIDC helper. OidcToken and
# IdentityTokens trade a cloud provider's identity token for a short-lived Whop access token and
# renew it using only OkHttp and Jackson, which the SDK already depends on. WhopOidc is the one
# part that touches generated code, and it depends on these generated symbols:
#   - WhopApiClientBuilder and AsyncWhopApiClientBuilder: their no-argument constructors, since
#     WhopOidc subclasses both; apiVersionDate(String), overridden to note a pinned version; the
#     protected setAuthentication hook, overridden; the protected setCustomHeaders hook,
#     overridden to call super and add Api-Version-Date when none is pinned; and the async
#     builder's protected buildClientOptions, overridden to call super and rebuild its options.
#   - core.ClientOptions: httpClient(), Builder.from, Builder.addHeader(String, Supplier),
#     Builder.addHeader(String, String), Builder.httpClient, Builder.timeout(Optional) and
#     Builder.build.
#   - core.LoggingInterceptor: the async builder drops the generated one, because rebuilding the
#     options appends another.
#   - types.ApiKeyApiVersionDate: its public static constants, read by reflection; the newest
#     toString() is the Api-Version-Date the builders send, so a regeneration moves it.
# A regeneration that renames a class or method above fails the helper's compile. Its tests live
# beside it so a regeneration cannot prune them; they also use WhopApiClient, AsyncWhopApiClient,
# users().retrieve, core.ILogger, core.LogConfig, core.LogLevel and ApiKeyApiVersionDate.Value.
src/main/java/com/whop/api/helpers/
src/test/java/com/whop/api/helpers/
